From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shelley Vohr <shelley.vohr@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 18:24:32 +0000
Subject: editing: don't recalc style from LayoutSelection::Commit()

LayoutSelection::Commit() runs from the compositing-inputs lifecycle
phase (the lifecycle is already at kInCompositingInputsUpdate) and
reaches FrameSelection::SelectionHasFocus() through IsHidden(), which
unconditionally forces Document::UpdateStyleAndLayout(). If style is
still dirty there - only DCHECKed in Commit() - the recalc
runs in a state where tree mutations are disallowed and the renderer
dies on CHECK(Lifecycle().StateAllowsTreeMutations()) in
Document::UpdateStyleAndLayoutTreeForThisDocument. In the field this is
a plain drag-select mouse-up crash (renderer, all desktop platforms).

Style can be dirty at that point without the lifecycle having rewound -
for example DocumentAnimations::NeedsAnimationTimingUpdate() becomes
true as soon as the animation clock has moved past the last style update
- and the lifecycle explicitly allows kVisualUpdatePending ->
kInCompositingInputsUpdate. Commit() only DCHECKed the assumption. When
the document needs a layout tree update, keep the selection pending and
schedule another frame so the next compositing-inputs step commits it
against clean style; the forced update inside SelectionHasFocus() is
then a guaranteed no-op on this path, and the clean path is unchanged.

Backport of https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8187581.

Bug: 541952000
Test: LayoutSelectionTest.CommitWithDirtyStyleRetriesNextFrame

(cherry picked from commit 3efe38516862c58899724803cde99db413589462)

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/layout_selection.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/layout_selection.cc
index 2ba06840c9ff94577a7dd6b90977809b8f83ce56..2e597ff938ee66bd107219279aa5810133905abf 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/layout_selection.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/layout_selection.cc
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/selection_template.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/visible_position.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/visible_units.h"
+#include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/local_frame_view.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/forms/text_control_element.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/html_wbr_element.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/block_node.h"
@@ -951,11 +952,21 @@ void LayoutSelection::SetHasPendingSelection() {
 void LayoutSelection::Commit() {
   if (!has_pending_selection_)
     return;
+
+  // CalcSelectionRangeAndSetSelectionState() reaches
+  // FrameSelection::SelectionHasFocus(), which updates style and layout. That
+  // is only safe as a no-op here: this runs in the compositing-inputs phase,
+  // where a real recalc CHECK-fails on StateAllowsTreeMutations(). Style can
+  // be dirty at this point without the lifecycle having rewound (e.g. an
+  // animation timing update became due), so commit on the next frame instead.
+  Document& document = frame_selection_->GetDocument();
+  if (document.NeedsLayoutTreeUpdate()) {
+    document.View()->ScheduleAnimation();
+    return;
+  }
   has_pending_selection_ = false;
 
-  DCHECK(!frame_selection_->GetDocument().NeedsLayoutTreeUpdate());
-  DCHECK_GE(frame_selection_->GetDocument().Lifecycle().GetState(),
-            DocumentLifecycle::kLayoutClean);
+  DCHECK_GE(document.Lifecycle().GetState(), DocumentLifecycle::kLayoutClean);
   DocumentLifecycle::DisallowTransitionScope disallow_transition(
       frame_selection_->GetDocument().Lifecycle());
 
